From 4d2c6fac6f7de0d64ed9b6d24eee28809dc56479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Joldersma <bennidhamma@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:14:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] [Ozone/Wayland] Support ext-background-effect-v1
 background blur

Bind ext_background_effect_manager_v1 when the compositor offers it
(COSMIC, Plasma 6.7+, Mutter 51+) and let windows request a blurred
backdrop behind translucent regions:

- BackgroundEffectManager wraps the global and tracks the blur
  capability, notifying windows when the compositor grants or revokes
  it.
- WaylandSurface keeps the blur region as double-buffered pending
  state alongside the opaque and input regions, creates the per-surface
  effect object lazily, and resends the region when the buffer scale
  changes. The region rounds outwards so thin rects that approximate
  rounded corners survive fractional scales.
- PlatformWindow::SetBackgroundBlurRegion() and
  PlatformWindowDelegate::OnBackgroundBlurSupportChanged() expose this
  to upper layers, and PlatformRuntimeProperties::
  supports_background_blur reports the capability.

Includes a fake-server implementation of the protocol and unit tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
